  "sourceNotes": [
    "Attempt SIX QUESTIONS is whole-examination selection. Retain every task in all eight questions, without duplicating six-question bundles.",
    "Q3(c)(ii) asks to verify one of the student’s own derived roots. No printed pool of answer options is offered. Keep one verification task, with both published verification examples and the prior-equation cap.",
    "Q4(c)(ii) Hence, or otherwise permits an alternative method; both real parameters are required.",
    "All requested table entries, sequence terms, roots, graph features and proofs are required, not optional selection pools.",
    "Mathematical errors/omissions lose 3; numerical slips and permitted misreadings lose 1.",
    "Relevant work earns at least the specified attempt award; worthless work earns 0. No marks strictly between zero and the attempt floor.",
    "Accept the best of multiple attempts unless specified otherwise; penalise the same error in one section once. Retain task-specific follow-through and caps.",
    "Published step awards remain separate score controls within a linked task. Alternative methods do not create extra cards or add marks.",
    "Independent visual sweep identifies 49 printed tasks, eight questions worth 50 marks each, 400 offered marks and 300 candidate marks.",
    "Q2(a), Q3(b)(i), Q3(c)(i), Q4(c)(ii), and Q6(c)(i) retain separately awarded steps inside their linked printed tasks.",
    "Q6(a)(i) period and range share one ten-mark award. Q8(i) is one fifteen-mark table-completion task; no separately published cell awards.",
    "The LC003GLP000EV.pdf paper filename is misleading: the original cover explicitly identifies 2011 M27 Ordinary Level Paper 1. The scheme with the same filename is a separate 104-page document, whose Paper 1 is pages 1–44.",
    "Q6(b)(ii) explains the omitted x = 0 domain restriction and preserves x ≠ 3 in the answer.",
    "Q7(b)(ii) explains the extra power in the original substitution definition.",
    "Q8(iv) explains the difference between the printed unbounded interval and the requested plotted domain."
